      "worked": "Replace $x$ with $x-a$ and $y$ with $y-b$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(x-a)^2+(x-a)(y-b)+(y-b)^2&=0\\\\x^2+xy+y^2-(2a+b)x-(a+2b)y+a^2+ab+b^2&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nEquating the coefficients of $x$ and $y$ gives\n$$\\begin{align*}2a+b&=-4\\\\a+2b&=-2.\\end{align*}$$\nTwice the second equation minus the first gives\n$$\\begin{align*}3b&=0\\\\b&=0\\\\a&=-2.\\end{align*}$$\nThe constant term also agrees:\n$$a^2+ab+b^2=(-2)^2+(-2)(0)+0^2=4.$$\nTherefore, the original relation was translated 2 units left, with no vertical translation.",
